  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree on NNN vertices and a positive integer KKK. Determine the maximum possible number of vertices you can choose so that the distance between any two of them is divisible by KKK.\n\nThe distance between two vertices is defined as the number of edges on the unique simple path between them.\n\n\nInput Format\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT −-− the number of test cases. The descriptions of TTT test cases follow.\n\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers NNN and KKK. Each of the next (N−1)(N-1)(N−1) lines contains two integers uuu, vvv (1≤u,v≤N1 \\le u, v \\le N1≤u,v≤N, u≠vu \\ne vu=v), denoting that there is an edge between vertices uuu and vvv. It is guaranteed that the described graph is a tree.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case output one integer −-− the maximum possible number of vertices you can choose so that the distance between any two of them is divisible by KKK.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤100 0001 \\le T \\le 100\\,0001≤T≤100000",
      "1≤K&lt;N≤500 0001 \\le K \\lt N \\le 500\\,0001≤K&lt;N≤500000",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases in one input does not exceed 1000 0001000\\,0001000000.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (15 points):** N≤1000N \\le 1000N≤1000, ∑N≤5000\\sum N \\le 5000∑N≤5000, KKK **is odd**.",
      "**Subtask 2 (20 points):** N≤1000N \\le 1000N≤1000, ∑N≤5000\\sum N \\le 5000∑N≤5000.",
      "**Subtask 3 (25 points):** N≤100 000N \\le 100\\,000N≤100000, ∑N≤200 000\\sum N \\le 200\\,000∑N≤200000, KKK **is odd**.",
      "**Subtask 4 (20 points):** N≤100 000N \\le 100\\,000N≤100000, ∑N≤200 000\\sum N \\le 200\\,000∑N≤200000.",
      "**Subtask 5 (10 points):** KKK **is odd**.",
      "**Subtask 6 (10 points):** no additional constraints."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
